    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk/HBlhIeSD#radK8osF",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "The history interface reads canonical states and their bound source declarations. Locality reports change frequency and coupling. Footprint compares explicit local refs and the selected proposal baseline, and lists each changed file that no binding holds, outside the vault. A named head that resolves in the vault's repository is read with the vault at that head, so its proposals and bindings come from the branch; the answer names the vault it read. Source refs lists the branches of every repository the state binds, merged by name. Each changed part names the other changed parts that its binding holds. Missing source stays unavailable rather than being reported as unchanged."
    },
    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk/XppR9owz#MrE3v2T6",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "The command passes explicit local source refs and selected architecture to the history interface. With --head on a ref that the vault's repository holds, it reads the vault at that head, so --state names a proposal of that branch. Proposal comparisons use their identified baseline. With --fail-outside and a draft, it exits 1 when the commits changed a module that the draft does not name, so a ticket merge without a pull request has a gate like the out-of-plan fail mode of the pull-request Action. A module bound to a directory passes when each file it changed lies in the binding of another changed module inside it."
    },
    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk/HBlhIeSD#nn1ec9Tw",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "Adapts canonical discovery, initialization, exact readings, archive history, branch readings at a source ref, and the existing change feed. Unmigrated vaults receive explicit migration guidance."
    },
    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk/yejBBUFY#w46oCRoH",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "Owns the reading address of a pane, including the source ref of a branch reading, so a branch reading survives reload and browser history."
    },
    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk#tQ2B3iEF",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "One history read of a revision answers for every part at once, and a selection shares it. A row selects its module on the picture. An unread part states why, and no count joins a score. A fourth view, What this branch changed, holds the branch footprint."
    },
